  <div class="container">
    <h1>What Unrecorded is and is not</h1>
    <p class="article-lead">
      Unrecorded is a local-first privacy awareness app for nearby Bluetooth signals
      that may match smart glasses or wearable recording devices.
    </p>

    <div class="disclaimer-box" role="note">
      <p><strong>Product truth:</strong> {{ site.productTruth }}</p>
    </div>

    <h2>What it is</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A privacy awareness tool for Android.</li>
      <li>A local scanner for Bluetooth Low Energy signals visible to your device.</li>
      <li>An explainable, rule-based risk indicator for patterns associated with known wearables.</li>
      <li>An open-source project that keeps scan processing on device by default.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What it is not</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>It is not proof that anyone is recording.</li>
      <li>It is not a camera, microphone, or lens detector.</li>
      <li>It is not a guarantee that every smart-glasses model will be noticed.</li>
      <li>It is not a cloud monitoring service, account system, or analytics product.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who it is for</h2>
    <p>
      Unrecorded is for people who want calmer situational awareness in public spaces,
      meetings, transit, classrooms, or other places where wearable recording devices
      may be present. It is also for developers and privacy advocates who want an
      inspectable detection model rather than a black box.
    </p>

